 :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos^{2} 40^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086630} {:answer/id #uuid "bf5edfab-7fe2-5720-9256-4fbe6a721e9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin 20^{∘}\\cos 20^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086631} {:answer/id #uuid "cfae1a0f-283c-5324-9b27-eacc1048da6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\cos 40^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086632} {:answer/id #uuid "1e5987d3-7bf9-5c07-b5ca-76df4ac6b2ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sin 20^{∘}\\cos 20^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086633} {:answer/id #uuid "34b6fd5d-0633-5cb7-b0e2-1c594186c2fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos 40^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfae1a0f-283c-5324-9b27-eacc1048da6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\cos 40^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086632} :answer-field/id #uuid "8393dfab-9f1b-5096-8134-b15c3fcf7ee2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086629}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9c84ae1b-25c3-565d-8730-075bec8eef99" :question/math-academy-id "q-7698" :question/problem "Express $5 - 10\\sin^{2} 20^{∘}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "Our expression can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n5(1-2{sin}^{2}⁡{20}^{∘})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={20}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2{sin}^{2}⁡{20}^{∘} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {20}^{∘})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{40}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n5(1-2{sin}^{2}⁡{20}^{∘})=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡{40}^{∘}.\n$$"}]}
